Counterfactual for koniz-dev/flutter-starter#127
================================================

What was changed, and only this: the `sessionSink:` argument was deleted from
`authInterceptorProvider` in lib/features/auth/di/auth_providers.dart, leaving
the interceptor with no way to reach the in-memory session - i.e. exactly the
pre-fix wiring described in the issue. Everything else, including the new
tests, is the shipped code.

Result: 3 of the 5 Tier-1 tests fail, and the acceptance golden test fails.
The two Tier-1 tests that still pass are invariants that held before the fix as
well (no DI cycle; a disposed container does not throw), which is why they are
kept - they guard the fix rather than demonstrate it.

The failure of the criterion-1 test is the defect in one line: after a 401
whose refresh failed, AuthState still holds `Instance of 'UserModel'` where
null was expected. The criterion-2 test reports the consequence: the router is
still on '/' rather than '/login'.

